  "body": "I vaguely recall @ayg complaining ages ago about duplicating the parsers we already have for ECMAScript and Web IDL. I think the idea against that was that HTML should in theory be able to go beyond the limits imposed by those parsers. That might still be a worthwhile goal of sorts, but I don't think there's a good reason to have multiple specifications define ConvertToInt and the like.",
